course: dictionary
lesson: 13086
title: Filth: dirt, germs and rude words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Filth is a noun that means very bad, disgusting dirt. «The bins behind the shop were full of filth, and the smell made everyone hold their noses.» The clues are the bins and the smell, so filth must be much worse than a bit of mud.
explain: Filth is uncountable, so you cannot count it. We do not say "a filth" or "two filths". We say «The room was covered in filth» or «They lived in filth.»
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Filth can also mean rude, offensive words or pictures. «The film was full of filth, so the teacher switched it off.» The clues tell you this is about rude content, not dirt.
fact: Filth means very bad, disgusting dirt.
fact: «Filth» is uncountable: say «some filth», not «a filth».
fact: Useful phrases: covered in filth, live in filth.
fact: Filth can also mean rude, offensive words, pictures or talk. This meaning is informal, so ask a teacher or adult if you are unsure.
fact: The slang «the filth» is an insulting word for the police. Do not use it, because it is rude and can hurt people.
exercise: «The boy came home covered in filth after playing in the mud.» What does filth mean here? | A kind of tasty food | Clean, fresh water | Shiny new clothes | *Very bad, disgusting dirt
exercise: Which sentence uses filth correctly? | He is a filth. | She saw a filth on the floor. | *The street was full of filth. | We bought three filths at the shop.
exercise: «The film was full of filth, so the teacher switched it off.» What kind of filth is this? | Old, torn cloth | Very dirty water | Rain and mud | *Rude, offensive talk or pictures
test: «The poor family lived in filth, with no clean water.» What does this tell you about their home? | They had no home at all | They lived in a palace | *It was very dirty and unhealthy | They had a very clean and tidy home
test: Which phrase is correct? | many filths | two filths | *covered in filth | a filth
exam: Why do doctors say to wash your hands after touching filth? | Filth makes your hands shiny | Dirt is good for your skin | Soap is only for washing dishes | *Germs in dirt can make you ill
